        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Xa0mfMo6snTwI4ojp3v2-76" value="" style="shape=tableRow;horizontal=0;startSize=0;swimlaneHead=0;swimlaneBody=0;strokeColor=inherit;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;collapsible=0;dropTarget=0;fillColor=none;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;fontSize=16;" vertex="1" parent="Xa0mfMo6snTwI4ojp3v2-75">
          <mxGeometry width="770" height="320" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Xa0mfMo6snTwI4ojp3v2-77" value="I added a few more attributes to the EMPLOYEE entity so it held more value. I also noticed that SALE_ITEM should only use a composite PK of SaleID and ItemID from the SALE and ITEM entities respectively, and remove the extra SALE_ITEM SaleItemID key completely. I also noticed I didn&#39;t follow naming convention for VENDOR_ITEM and it&#39;s relationship was listed backwards. This is because I was following Parent-Child with SALE_ITEM, the SALE contains the ITEM. Naturally I was thinking VENDOR_ITEM, because you buy the item from the vendor, but in the view or perspective of the database itself, it&#39;s the ITEM is supplied by what vendors? This ITEM_VENDOR format puts the ITEM entity as the parent or primary focus, which from this database stand point, it is. I also added VendorItemCost and PreferredVendor to ITEM_VENDOR because you can track and compare items from multiple vendors in this fashion and then set which vendor is the preferred vendor for certain items. For instance, vendor &#39;a&#39; sells chairs for $25 each, vendor &#39;b&#39; sells the same chairs for $35 each within the same month of October as per their PurchaseDate value. A job query can run where it finds the lowest value purchase for that item within a time period and adjusts the value of PreferredVendor. This allows you to just sort the list with the lowest value on top, set PreferredVendor to Yes and then set the rest to No. This can change over time, so that gives more weight to PurchaseDate along with maintaining inventory purchase records as a whole." style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=none;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=16;rowspan=1;colspan=3;" vertex="1" parent="Xa0mfMo6snTwI4ojp3v2-76">
          <mxGeometry width="770" height="320" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="257" height="320" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Xa0mfMo6snTwI4ojp3v2-78" value="" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=none;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=16;" visible="0" vertex="1" parent="Xa0mfMo6snTwI4ojp3v2-76">
          <mxGeometry x="257" width="256" height="320" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="256" height="320" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
